################################################################################
 THREAT: Junk email (spam content and bulk mail flood)
################################################################################
 Description   : Unsolicited bulk mail: spam/phishing content, and high-volume sending from one source.
 Why relevant  : The mail server is how operators get alerts and talk to users; spam is the main carrier of phishing/fraud, and a flood fills the queue, the disk and the spamd workers.
 Exploitation  : Anyone who can reach port 25 can submit mail (no authentication for local recipients); before the hardening the whole lab /24 was trusted and could relay.
 Monitoring    : Wazuh reads /var/log/mail.log: 100220 spamd 'identified spam', 100223 Postfix 'hold' (quarantine), 100221 accepted message per client IP, 100222 = 10 messages in 30 s from the same srcip.
 Action-resp.  : Spam content: quarantined in the Postfix hold queue (header_checks). Flood: firewall-drop of the sender IP for 60 s. Relay: refused by Postfix (mynetworks = localhost only).
